  "published": "2026-11-23T09:56:01.207Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.1.4: faster and lighter saves with the same output, byte for byte (a 1,000-row table, warm: about 136 ms to 55 ms and 59 MB to 18.5 MB allocated per save). Printable ASCII is shaped word by word with a per-font word cache in fonts whose layout rules never involve the space, glyph positions are written without the custom number format, layout arrays are pooled, and ASCII text skips the general Unicode passes it does not need. The guide has a new section on startup time (ReadyToRun: a first save in a fresh process about a third faster).\n\n0.1.3: a zero width joiner or non-joiner at the end of a line is no longer missing from the extracted text; text shaping and layout are faster and allocate less (a 1,000-row table: about 82 MB to 59 MB per save); the output is unchanged.\n\n0.1.2: PdfImage.FromBytes reads WebP pictures (lossy, lossless and with alpha; an animated WebP is refused), decoded in managed code with no new dependency. Files are much smaller (a 1,000-row table: 514 KB to 76 KB) with the same glyph positions, and writing a page allocates about half as much; the text reads back as before in PdfPig and pdf.js.\n\n0.1.1: a line break or another control character in a string no longer makes a save throw. Every line break (\\n, \\r\\n, \\r, U+0085, U+000B, U+000C, U+001C to U+001E, U+2028, U+2029) is a hard line break inside the same block, everywhere text is laid out (canvas text included); other control characters are removed; a lone surrogate becomes U+FFFD; metadata, font family and language strings are trimmed and cleaned. Text without these characters is written as before.\n\n0.1.0, the first release: a PDF writer for reports. Blocks (Heading, Paragraph, Table, ItemList, Columns, Callout, Drawing, Image) flow and paginate; tables stream their rows and repeat the header; a drawing canvas and a text measurer serve charts; headers and footers know the page count; fonts are supplied by the caller and embedded as subsets; right-to-left and mixed-direction text, and Arabic, Hebrew, Devanagari, Bengali, Tamil and Thai shaping through HarfBuzz, are written in logical order so the text can be searched and copied; output is deterministic; SaveAsync can be cancelled; PdfImageOptions limits picture size (40 megapixels by default).\n\nKnown limitations (0.1.x): the language review of the test text was made by an AI agent, not by native speakers (Tamil, Bengali, Thai and Marathi least certain); the viewer check was PDFium renders, and Acrobat Reader and macOS Preview were not checked; the output-size target is met but the speed and memory targets are missed (docs/baselines.md); CJK fonts with TrueType outlines are accepted but not tested, and fonts with CFF outlines (Noto Sans CJK, Source Han) are not supported yet.\n\nFull notes: https://github.com/sinanoran/pdfwright/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md",
